# TRIAGE environment template. Copy to `.env`, keep ONE profile.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROFILE A - FULLY LOCAL, ZERO API KEYS  (default below; nothing phones home)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   generator : ollama llama3.1:8b      (~5 GB VRAM, free)
#   judge     : ollama qwen2.5:14b      (~9 GB Q4; drop to qwen2.5:7b if tight)
#   JEV gate  : local calibrated mode   (no TYPESAFE_API_KEY => automatic)
#   telemetry : local JSON + figures    (no W&B)
#
# Prereqs on the target machine:
#   ollama pull llama3.1:8b && ollama pull qwen2.5:14b
#   pip install -r requirements.txt + the two scispacy URLs (see README)
#   public HF model downloads (SapBERT) work anonymously; no token required
#
LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
JUDGE_OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:14b
WANDB_MODE=disabled

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PROFILE B - CLOUD JUDGE + ONLINE TELEMETRY (opt-in upgrades, uncomment+fill)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx                # judge auth for the profile below
# JUDGE_PROVIDER=huggingface     # judge => Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct (HF cloud,
#                                 # pay-per-token ~$2 per 50-sample run; paper parity)
# WANDB_API_KEY=                 # + remove WANDB_MODE=disabled => runs stream online
# WANDB_PROJECT=hcad-rag
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=              # live JEV System One gate (else local calibrated mode)
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=                # NIM fallback provider if ollama is unavailable

# Model overrides (defaults are sensible):
# LLM_NVIDIA_MODEL=meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct
# JUDGE_NVIDIA_MODEL=qwen/qwen2.5-72b-instruct
